      "commentary": "17:17-24 The widow and Elijah are tested. Another crisis gives YHWH the opportunity to show He is in control of death!\n\nWhen the Bible speaks on this subject, we must clarify three types of YHWH's power over death.\n\n- Enoch and Elijah are taken to heaven without death.\n\n- The son and many others are restored to physical life but they will die again in the future (i.e., resuscitation).\n\n- Jesus was resurrected, which means a new spiritual/physical existence (i.e., no more death). Jesus is the only one so far\n(cf. 1 Corinthians 15).\n\nThis resuscitation would have been related to the myth of Ba'al's death and rising (i.e., winter-spring).\nBa'al had no power over death (as he had no power over rain) but YHWH did!\n\n17:17 \"no breath left in him\" This is the ancient's belief that \"breath\" showed life; no breath (BDB 675), no life.\nThis is not the word ruah (BDB 924) but a SYNONYM.\n\nNotice in v. 22 the child's nephesh returns to him. For nephesh (BDB 659) see notes\nonline at Gen. 35:18 and Lev. 17:11."
