      "commentary": "17:19 \"the upper room\" This was a structure on the roof which could be reached by stairs on the outside of the house.\nIt was possibly used only in the hot months by the family.\n\nThe term (BDB 751; NIDOTTE, vol. 3, p. 422) is used in a variety of ways.\n\n- upper room of a modest home ‒ here\n\n- upper room of a palace ‒ Jdgs. 3:20; 2 Kgs. 1:2; Isa. 28:8\n\n- upper floor of the temple ‒ 1 Chr. 28:11; 2 Chr. 3:9\n\n- upper room over a city's gate ‒ 2 Sam. 19:1\n\n- even of YHWH's dwelling place ‒ Ps. 104:3,13"
